# Ziggurat decision-archive schedule (item 4.2b) — systemd USER timer.
#
# TUESDAY 18:30 box-local (this box runs Pacific). Three things fix that slot:
#
#   1. AFTER the 17:15 PT league sync. The plan reads today's rosters and today's
#      free-agent pool; the sync that lands them is the 17:15 run (17:19 observed).
#      Firing before it would archive yesterday's league state under today's date.
#   2. BEFORE the operator's evening. 19:00-21:00 PT is unavailable, and the
#      claims have to be queued in the app before ~23:59 PT to make that night's
#      batch (the batch runs 00:01-01:13 PT, measured, item 3.8a). A capture at
#      18:30 is the last undisturbed snapshot of the pool before the league's
#      other managers start acting on it.
#   3. It is a SECOND capture, never the only one. Every `ziggurat waivers` run
#      captures too, so on a Tuesday the operator actually works, this unit adds
#      one more directory (~450 KB) and the record command names which capture the
#      submitted claims belong to. That is the intended cost.
#
# Persistent=true, and what a catch-up MEANS here: a Tuesday capture that fires
# on Wednesday is a WEDNESDAY decision — the pool has re-formed after the
# overnight waiver batch, so it archives a different world under a later
# `as_of`. It is still worth having (it is the only record of that morning), and
# `captured_at` plus `plan_as_of` in the manifest are what tell the two apart.
# Nothing is ever back-stamped.
#
# RandomizedDelaySec is deliberately absent: nothing else contends for this slot,
# and the ordering against the 17:15 sync is the whole point of the hour.

[Unit]
Description=Ziggurat decision-archive schedule (Tuesday, pre-submission freeze)
Documentation=file://@REPO@/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Tue *-*-* 18:30:00
Persistent=true
AccuracySec=1m
Unit=ziggurat-decisions.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
